<h3 id="kinemaster">In KineMaster</h3>
<p>Select the clip › <b>Adjustment</b>: Temperature = Warmth, Contrast, Saturation, Highlights, Shadows; use <b>Lift</b> for Fade (+5 to +15). KineMaster has no grain slider — add <code>grain_H.png</code> / <code>grain_V.png</code> from the assets as a layer at 15–30% opacity. Save time: adjust one clip, then copy-paste the adjustment to the others.</p>
<h3 id="picsart">In PicsArt</h3>
<p><b>Tools › Adjust</b>: Temperature, Contrast, Saturation, Highlights, Shadows, Vignette. Fade is under <b>Tools › Curves</b> (drag the bottom-left point up a little) or <b>Effects › Fade</b>. Grain: <b>Effects › Grain</b>, or the grain PNG at 20%. Save it with <b>Replay</b> so the next photo gets the same look in one tap.</p>
<h3 id="lightroom">In Lightroom mobile</h3>
<p>The signature, exactly: Temp +6, Tint +2, Contrast +10, Highlights −12, Shadows +10, Whites −4, Blacks +8, Vibrance +8, Saturation −4. Colour grading — Shadows hue 200 sat 10, Highlights hue 35 sat 12, Balance +10. HSL — Green sat −15 lum −5, Orange sat −5 lum +5, Red sat +5. Grain 15 / size 25 / roughness 50. Save as a preset called <em>imswarnil</em>.</p>
<h3 id="apple-photos">In Apple Photos (iPhone)</h3>
<p>Brilliance +10, Highlights −15, Shadows +10, Contrast +8, Brightness +3, Black Point −10, Saturation −3, Vibrance +8, Warmth +10, Tint +2, Vignette +10. Copy Edits, then Paste Edits onto the rest of the batch.</p>

<h2 id="matching">Matching a look across a post</h2>
<ul>
	<li><b>Match the light, then the look.</b> First make the photos agree on exposure and white balance (a face should be the same brightness in all of them), then apply the same look to all. A LUT on mismatched photos only makes the mismatch prettier.</li>
	<li><b>Skin first.</b> Judge every look on a face. If skin turns orange or grey, back the Warmth or the strength off before anything else.</li>
	<li><b>Leave the red alone.</b> One true red stays in every frame — a dot, a chip, a jacket. If a look dulls it, raise Red saturation (+5) in HSL.</li>
	<li><b>Words never get the look.</b> Headline type stays pure white or pure ink; add the type <em>after</em> the grade, on its own layer.</li>
	<li><b>Grain last, and the same everywhere.</b> Grain is what makes a phone photo and a camera photo sit together in one feed.</li>
</ul>
